### 1\. Product definition

NetFusion will be a multi-network management application with four main subsystems.

* Network Manager: Detects, monitors and manages multiple internet connections.

* Load Balancer: Distributes different application sessions across available connections.

* Streaming Optimizer: Prioritizes video, live streaming, gaming and video conferencing.

* Bonding Engine: Combines multiple independent network paths through an optional relay.

### Important technical distinction

The optional relay determines which features are possible:

| Feature                                            | Without relay | With relay                              |
| -------------------------------------------------- | ------------- | --------------------------------------- |
| Network monitoring                                 | Yes           | Yes                                     |
| Load balancing                                     | Yes           | Yes                                     |
| Failover                                           | Yes           | Yes                                     |
| Streaming prioritization                           | Yes           | Yes                                     |
| Different downloads on different paths             | Yes           | Yes                                     |
| Combining one ordinary download across connections | Generally no  | Yes, with supported multipath transport |
| Combined public internet exit                      | No            | Yes                                     |

The Windows PC will be the local gateway. It will accept connections from Android and Windows clients over the LAN and forward their traffic through the selected upstream connections.

A local server does not itself create additional bandwidth. True bonding requires a compatible endpoint on the other side of the internet paths.

