### 10\. Streaming and QoS implementation

The streaming engine should use five traffic categories.

### NetFusion traffic priority model

P0 – Real-time

100/100

Video calls and interactive audio

P1 – Gaming

90/100

Online and cloud gaming

P2 – Video

70/100

YouTube, OTT and video playback

P3 – Normal

50/100

Browsing and general apps

P4 – Background

30/100

Downloads and updates

These are initial scheduling weights, not guaranteed bandwidth percentages.

### Scheduling logic

The scheduler should consider:

* Current available bandwidth.

* Latency.

* Jitter.

* Packet loss.

* Connection stability.

* Traffic category.

* Existing flow assignments.

It should avoid switching an active TCP flow between interfaces unless the routing architecture can preserve that flow.

For encrypted streaming traffic, automatic identification may be uncertain. NetFusion should support manual application selection and user-configured rules.

### 11\. Bonding engine implementation

This is the most important advanced subsystem.

### Recommended approach

Start with multiple independent QUIC tunnels:

```text
                 Windows Client
                       |
                 Bonding Manager
                       |
           +-----------+-----------+
           |           |           |
        Tunnel 1    Tunnel 2    Tunnel 3
           |           |           |
          Jio        Airtel       Wi-Fi
           |           |           |
           +-----------+-----------+
                       |
                Remote Relay
                       |
                    Internet
```

The bonding manager must handle:

* Tunnel creation.

* Path health.

* Packet scheduling.

* Packet identifiers.

* Reordering.

* Loss recovery.

* Retransmission.

* Flow control.

* Session authentication.

The receiving relay reassembles the data before forwarding it.

Development rule: Do not build a new cryptographic protocol. Use established TLS/QUIC security and concentrate your implementation work on path scheduling, sequencing and recovery.

For the first release, keep this module disabled. The rest of NetFusion should remain fully useful without it.

